and what does that mean?

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.149
What is Ramsay Hunt syndrome mean?

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.151
Yeah, so it can be challenging

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.654
to diagnose encephalitis, encephalitis

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.455
basically means inflammation

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.256
of the brain.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.325
People often hear meningitis

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.893
that is inflammation of the layers,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.395
the outside layers of the brain.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.563
But with encephalitis,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.530
you're actually getting swelling

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.832
in several different areas of the brain.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.734
Now, it can be challenging to diagnose.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.403
Usually you have some suspicion.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.304
As Monty mentioned,

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.005
she had diagnosed shingles.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:26.439
Shingles

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.441
can sometimes lead to

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.543
encephalitis, inflammation of the brain.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.711
You have several tests

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.612
that you start to do

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.080
to try and figure that out.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.150
Imaging tests, for example, EEG

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.718
electroencephalogram

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.752
would be another test

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.654
and even a lumbar puncture

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.423
where you'd actually look at fluid

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.991
that bathes the spinal cord

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.125
in the brain and see,

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.060
look, is the virus

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.795
and there are indications

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.830
that there is a swelling and inflammation

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.165
around the brain.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.933
That's how you'd make that diagnosis.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.801
Sometimes it's hard.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:55.835
People have fever.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.503
They may have headache

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.405
sometimes those symptoms are resolve,

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.107
but people may be left with memory

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.108
sort of difficulties.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.177
So it can be challenging, Jake.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.678
And what about Ramsey Hunt?

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.746
What is that?

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.581
So so when someone has shingles

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.882
and a lot of people know what shingles

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.818
is, typically it's a virus

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.052
that you may have had chickenpox

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:13.886
when you were a child.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.389
Even the virus doesn't leave your body.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.490
It stays sort of

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.225
hanging out around nerves

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.027
at some point in adult life.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.396
It can get reactivated that shingles,

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.632
if that reactivation occurs

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.166
around the face

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.835
and specifically around the facial nerve.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.236
And I think we have an image here

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.372
of what the facial nerve sort of. Yes.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.407
That yellow area there, the facial nerve.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.276
If that becomes inflamed,

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.311
as a result of the virus,

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.812
you can develop

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.681
a weakness of that side of the face.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.316
You can develop lesions

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.717
even inside the ear.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:45.785
Difficulty with hearing,

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.886
difficulty with vision.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.154
It can be inside your mouth.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.756
It can be very painful.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.024
People who have had shingles

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.625
know how painful it can be.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.326
Imagine that

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.328
same sort of thing happening on your face

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:57.530
and possibly affecting the nerve

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.599
that gives your face. It's movement.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:02.068
It can resolve if it's treated early

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.303
and it's typically treated

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.205
with steroids and antiviral medications.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.107
If it's recognized early and treated

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.542
early, people can resolve,

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.010
but it can take a while.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:11.577
By the way, Jake,

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.712
just quickly, it's different

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.147
than Bell's Palsy.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.014
With Bell's palsy,

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.549
you can get similar symptoms

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.317
We don't always know

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.052
what causes Bell's palsy.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.620
With this Ramsey Hunt,

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.854
it's almost always that virus

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.989
that causes shingles.

